WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.467
-I've been very excited
to see you.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.634
I love seeing you.
-I love seeing you, too.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:06.634
-Yeah, I -- I want to get into
your two movies.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.934
They're giant movies.
You're -- You're the --

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.334
You're the Hollywood
"it girl" right now.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:11.901
-Am I?
-Yeah, I said so.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.067
-That's nice to say.

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:14.801
-I want to ask you a question.
This is serious.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:16.367
-[ Somber voice] Okay.
What is it, Jimmy?

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:17.467
-I heard --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:20.100
-Yes?
-I heard that you like --

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.667
I heard that you like
to crash weddings,

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:22.968
and I just think
that's interesting.

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.133
-Oh, well --
That is interesting.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:29.667
It's interesting you say that.
I did that once.

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.467
-But you don't -- like, that's
not a thing that you do?

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.434
-Well, a friend of mine,
we were in the same place.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:38.133
And I was, like -- I was
in Italy with my sisters.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:42.033
And in Italy, they have --
they have a lot of wine there.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:43.601
[ Laughter ]
And...

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.534
-So that was your invite
right there, huh?

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:48.000
-So that -- they --
my friend was at this wedding.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.834
And he's like, "Just come.
It's a really big wedding.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:52.434
No one will know."
And then, all of a sudden,

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.934
I'm just making eye contact
with the bride

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.334
as she's being
bounced in a chair.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:01:00.734
[ Laughter ]
And she was like...

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.067
-Yeah.
-"What?"

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:03.834
-That's pretty fun.
-"Why is she here?"

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:04.868
-That's cool, though.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:06.734
"Dakota Johnson's
at my wedding."

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.534
-I'm a nice person to --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.000
-I know you are!
Yeah.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.167
But I mean -- But so that's --
I'm sorry, I thought that was

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.701
the story, that you crash
weddings, you crash parties.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.901
-No. Well, like, the other night
in here, actually,

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.901
I was just at dinner
with friends and they were like,

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:23.467
"We're going to a birthday party
at Electric Lady."

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:25.901
So I went to that.
-And you --

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.300
you weren't really
invited to that, either?

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.033
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.367
No, I wasn't.
But it actually

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:33.033
wasn't even a birthday party.
It was a staff party.

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:34.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:35.634
-That's even crazier.
But then -- But then --

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:36.934
-Yeah.
-So maybe you do --

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.801
-They were really like,
"What are you doing here?"

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:40.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.667
-Maybe you do crash things
and you don't think about it.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:46.501
Is there any other scam?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:48.767
-Was I invited to this show?
-Oh, my goodness!

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.133
[ Laughter ]
You were --

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.434
You are always invited
to this show.

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:53.200
We love you.
-Thanks.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.300
-I want to talk about --
You have two movies.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.901
Two big movies.
Let's get right to it.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:59.968
"Persuasion" is coming out
July 15th, on Netflix.

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:03.167
It's a Jane Austen adaptation.

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:06.901
You're wearing gorgeous dresses,
running around -- yep.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:08.667
I love Jane Austen.
-Me too.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.100
-[ British accent ]
I really liked it because

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.100
I do, um...
-Accents.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.267
-Yeah, I do.
How'd you know?

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.367
-That's really good, yeah.
-Is it?

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:18.267
Is it, though?
Is it -- Is it good?

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.667
[ Laughter ]
-I don't know.

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:21.267
-Is it all right?
-Not really.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:22.534
-Yeah, not really.
-No.

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.200
-I do accents
every now and then.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.400
I can do a different one.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.934
And I'm just saying,
I could audition.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:29.534
I could be in the next movie
that you want to be in."

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:30.934
-[ Laughing ] Are you okay?

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:33.300
-[ Normal voice ]
That's -- That's the reaction

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.167
I want from people --
"Are you okay?"

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.234
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:37.934
-He's transformed.

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.734
-Are you great -- but are you
good with accents?

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:41.501
Do you love doing them?
-I love doing them.

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:44.501
I had an amazing vocal coach
for "Persuasion," though.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.400
Jill McCullough.
And then, her assistant,

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.167
Helen Simmons,
was on set with me.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.601
-Yeah.
-And we would do, like,

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:54.200
crazy warm-ups in the mornings
at like 5:00 in the morning.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.133
-Whoa.
-Which would be hard-core.

00:02:56.133 --> 00:03:00.534
So we'd make them
really, really naughty.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.067
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:04.334
Okay. Just to try
and keep it interesting

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:05.901
at 5:00 in the morning?
-Yeah.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:07.267
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-What else are you gonna do

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:09.567
except say a bunch of, like,
really gnarly words.

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.567
-Is there any ones you can say
on television?

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:14.667
-Yeah.
One of them was like,

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.534
"Look at the lovely lemons
in the lounge."

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:17.667
-Wow.

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:19.367
[ British accent ]
Look -- Look at the --

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.234
[ Laughter ]
Hey! Oi!

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.100
Look at the lovely lemons
on the lounge.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.767
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.267
Yeah.
-I'm telling you, I'm available.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:31.400
-Or like, "Please put the tiny
cup on the kitchen top."

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.634
-Please put a cup on the tea --
on the top.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:35.934
[ Laughter ]
Please put a cup --

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:38.267
Hey, put a cup on the tea!

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:40.133
Put a --
-It's Mick Jagger.

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:41.300
-[ Normal voice ]
Mick Jagger, yeah.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.033
I'm just saying I can do that.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.467
If you need that in your film,
you know --

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:46.567
-That's what I need.
-You know who to call.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.534
I'm your guy.
But, congrats.

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.667
Let's talk about
"Cha Cha Real Smooth."

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:52.767
-Yes.
-I love -- I love the title.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.067
-You got it right.
-Of course.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.400
-Yeah.
-"Cha Cha Real Smooth."

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.467
I know that jam. It's in
theaters and on Apple TV+.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:01.734
It's -- You're getting
rave reviews for this.

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:04.200
How do we set this up?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.167
-This is my company, TeaTime's,
first movie that we made.

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:13.000
We developed it from an idea
that the director,

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.601
Cooper Raiff, brought to us.

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:20.267
It's about a young man
who leaves college

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.334
and doesn't have a job,
doesn't really know what to do

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:23.968
with himself,
and he becomes a party starter

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:26.601
at bar mitzvahs
and bat mitzvahs.

00:04:26.601 --> 00:04:28.033
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:33.234
-And he meets a young mother
of -- of, like, a 14-year-old

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.501
autistic girl
and falls in love with her.

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.300
-Yeah.
It's -- It's a sweet story.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.434
And "Cha Cha Real Smooth,"
why is that the title?

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:43.033
Just 'cause --
-Well, you know,

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:45.200
in the "Cha-Cha Slide"...
-Yeah.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.734
-...the part of the song --

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:47.968
This --
Cooper came up with this,

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:50.534
and it's annoying
because it's really good.

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:51.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:53.501
But, yeah.
-You wanted credit for it?

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:56.234
-Yeah.
I'm on TV right now,

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:58.000
so I'm gonna take credit for it.
-Yeah.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.467
-He said -- No, I say,
it's the part of the song

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:04.200
where you do your own dance.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.033
-Oh, yeah.
Because he tells you the --

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:07.801
-"Cha-Cha now, y'all."
-Yeah.

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:09.801
-And then
you do your own boogie.

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:12.934
-Yeah, so this is his part
of his life where he's like,

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:14.501
"This is the part
where I do my own thing."

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:16.100
-Yeah.
-Yeah, it's a good title.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.968
I will say, congrats.

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:19.934
It won the
Audience Award at Sundance.

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:22.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
And it was one of

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.601
the biggest sellers
out of Sundance.

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:25.901
Big hit.
-Yeah.

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:27.467
-Big, successful.
Congratulations.

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:28.667
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:30.934
Here's Dakota Johnson
in "Cha Cha Real Smooth."

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:32.367
Take a look at this.

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:36.667
-On the Earth, we all have,
like, a ton of soul mates.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.901
And I think for you, maybe,
it's like a special case

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:41.968
where you only have a few...
-[ Chuckles ]

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:48.133
...who, like, could be and
really are your soul mates.

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:50.634
But most of the people in the
world aren't your soul mates.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.567
-How many soul mates?

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:54.667
-For you?
Like, four.

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:56.934
-Four?
-Yeah, four soul mates.

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.300
-I probably
haven't met any of them.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.367
-No, you have.
God puts them, like,

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:03.734
on your path so you'll cross.
-How many do you have?

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:07.767
-Like 1,200.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:14.501
-Have you met any?
-Yes.

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.200
Domino, domino, domino.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.667
-[ Gasps ]
[ Crashing, body thuds ]

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:20.734
Oh, my God. That's a ton
of blood right away.

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:23.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.400
-"Oh, my God. That's a ton
of blood right away."

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.534
Dakota Johnson, everybody!
"Cha Cha Real Smooth"

00:06:28.534 --> 00:06:31.767
is in theaters
and on Apple TV+ this Friday.

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:34.133
Dakota and I are doing
"Mad Lib Karaoke"

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:35.634
when we come back.
Stick around.

